Advertise CUDA registration on IB when dmabuf is available.

SCOPE AND SAFETY -- this patch is DEFAULT ON (opt out with DAOS_IB_DMABUF_CUDA=0),
unlike its companion mercury-0001, which is opt-in for a reason.

It is measured harmless. The configuration that passed
tests/test_rawio_integrity.py 80/80 (28 MiB, 16 threads) on client-6 had THIS
patch active and mercury-0001's CUDA components disabled via
NA_UCX_EXTRA_TLS=. So advertising CUDA registrability on the memory domain
does not by itself disturb host-memory transfers; adding cuda_copy/cuda_ipc to
the UCX TLS list does, and that is the other patch.

Record the validated combination, because only this one has been tested:

    ucx-0001      : enabled  (default)
    mercury-0001  : disabled (NA_UCX_EXTRA_TLS unset or empty)
    result        : raw DFS I/O byte-exact, 80/80

Both patches exist only to make dfs_read_gpu()/dfs_write_gpu() work, and
gpudirect/PLAN.md records the decision not to build the GPU-direct backend. If
you enable the CUDA components, re-run test_rawio_integrity.py and require a
clean pass first -- the failure mode is silent corruption, not an error.

diff --git a/src/uct/ib/base/ib_md.c b/src/uct/ib/base/ib_md.c
index 265d53e0a..a3a80a2e0 100644
--- a/src/uct/ib/base/ib_md.c
+++ b/src/uct/ib/base/ib_md.c
@@ -1248,6 +1248,24 @@ static void uct_ib_md_check_dmabuf(uct_ib_md_t *md)
 
     ucs_debug("%s: dmabuf is supported", uct_ib_device_name(&md->dev));
     md->cap_flags |= UCT_MD_FLAG_REG_DMABUF;
+
+    /* On platforms that have no legacy peer-memory driver (nvidia_peermem or
+     * nv_peer_mem), uct_ib_check_gpudirect_driver() leaves CUDA out of
+     * reg_mem_types because it only probes those sysfs paths. ucp_mem_map()
+     * with UCS_MEMORY_TYPE_CUDA then fails with -EIO even though the device
+     * can register GPU memory through a dma-buf FD -- which is the path
+     * ibv_reg_dmabuf_mr() takes, and which we verified works on this HCA.
+     * Advertise CUDA when dmabuf is available. Set DAOS_IB_DMABUF_CUDA=0 to
+     * restore the upstream behaviour. */
+    {
+        const char *dmabuf_cuda = getenv("DAOS_IB_DMABUF_CUDA");
+
+        if ((dmabuf_cuda == NULL) || strcmp(dmabuf_cuda, "0")) {
+            md->reg_mem_types |= UCS_BIT(UCS_MEMORY_TYPE_CUDA);
+            ucs_debug("%s: advertising cuda registration via dmabuf",
+                      uct_ib_device_name(&md->dev));
+        }
+    }
 #endif
 }
 
